# Core feature slice

Platform-agnostic — no JSX, no `react-native`, no `expo-*`, no `@repo/tokens`.
ESLint enforces this; never add `eslint-disable`.

## File order

1. `schemas.ts` — zod schemas, `z.infer` for types
2. `api.ts` — one function per endpoint, `Schema.parse(response.data)`
3. `keys.ts` — key factory, never inline arrays
4. `hooks.ts` — TanStack Query hooks
5. `index.ts` — barrel

## zod v4 syntax

```ts
z.email(); // not z.string().email()
z.iso.datetime(); // not z.string().datetime()
z.infer<typeof schema>; // derive type, never hand-write interface
```

## TanStack Query v5 syntax

```ts
useQuery({ queryKey: xKeys.detail(id), queryFn: () => getX(id) });
// No positional overloads — object syntax only
```

`staleTime`/`gcTime` are set once in `packages/core/src/query/client.ts`. Do not
repeat them on every hook; override one only when that resource really differs,
with a comment saying why (see `profileOptions`).

## Cross-field validation

```ts
.superRefine((val, ctx) => {
  if (condition) ctx.addIssue({ code: 'custom', path: ['fieldName'], message: '...' });
})
// NOT .refine() — it puts errors at form root, not on the field
```
